From 967b605d3882527b7c69fa3d2274ab5dd5a821fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BrenOne <vertkey2006@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:36:21 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Stable USB, full brightness, 60 FPS, corner-aware layout

- Frames use the official 1-based (start,r,g,b,end) range format, merged to
  at most 34 ranges (3 HID reports instead of 8), 1 ms gap between reports
- Retry/reopen a stalled hid_write (0x3E5) instead of dropping the strip
- Read LED count and size via 0x82 and adopt them automatically
- Hardware brightness 255 (was 100 on a 0-255 scale)
- 45/60 FPS options, 60 by default
- Per-side LED counts and corner gap for strips with empty corners
- Turn the strip off on Windows shutdown/restart/sign-out

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017Sqdi9StAk5iH4ETYHDqEq
